course: dictionary
lesson: 12818
title: Embodied: showing an idea, including a part, having a body
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Embodied is the past form of the verb embody. Its first meaning is to show an idea or quality so clearly that a person or thing seems to be a perfect example of it. «Maya embodied kindness when she shared her lunch with everyone.» Maya is kindness in action, so embodied means showed kindness clearly.
explain: Its second meaning is to include something as a part of a bigger thing. «The fair play rule is embodied in the school's first law.» The rule is part of the law. Look for clue words like in or the spirit of, which often point to this meaning.
explain: In science, especially AI and robots, embodied means having a body that acts in the real world. «The embodied robot rolled across the floor and felt each bump.» A robot with no body can only think or speak; an embodied robot can move and sense things.
fact: Embody means to show an idea or quality clearly, or to include it as a part of something.
fact: The past forms are embodied (past) and embodying (present participle); embodies is used with he, she or it.
fact: «Embodied» can mean showing a quality, such as «embodied courage», or being included, such as «embodied in a law».
fact: «Embodied» in science means having a physical body that can act and sense in the real world.
fact: Phrases to know: «embodied the spirit of» means showed that spirit clearly, and «embodied in» means included in.
exercise: «The hero embodied courage when she ran into the burning hall to save the baby.» What does embodied mean here? | *Showed courage clearly, as a perfect example | Left the hall quickly | Counted the rooms | Was afraid of the fire
exercise: «The rules embodied in the school charter are fair to all.» What does embodied mean here? | Painted in bright colours | Thrown away and forgotten | Read out loud twice | *Included as part of the rules
exercise: «The embodied robot could feel the bumps on the floor.» What does embodied suggest? | It can only speak | It is very old | It is made of paper | *It has a body that acts in the real world
test: «Grandma embodied patience while she taught me to knit.» What does embodied mean? | *Showed patience clearly, as a perfect example | Was cross with the wool | Broke the knitting needles | Forgot all about patience
test: Which is the past form of embody? | embody | embodies | embodying | *embodied
exam: «The team embodied the spirit of the school: they never gave up and they helped each other.» What does embodied mean? | Argued with the school | *Showed the spirit of the school clearly, as a perfect example | Forgot the spirit of the school | Left the school early
